# Private working notes. These carry real account, organization, and SCP
# identifiers, so they stay local. The IDs are recorded in .env, and the
# committed documents under docs/ write them as ${PLACEHOLDER} instead.
#
# Everything load-bearing has been lifted out of these files and into docs/,
# so a fresh clone is missing evidence, never a conclusion.
support/
*.local.md

# Secrets and credentials
# Nothing in this repo should ever carry AWS keys or a Vocareum token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
bedrock-key/bedrock-key.env
.envrc
secrets.json
credentials
*credential*
*creds*
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.pem
*.ppk
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# Vocareum's live AWS-session SSH private key. The broader *.key rule above
# already covers it; keep the exact name visible so it is never mistaken for a
# repository fixture.
student.key
.aws/
.aws-sam/
aws-exports.js
*token*.txt
*secret*.txt
.netrc
.pypirc
.npmrc

# bedrock-key/create-key.py writes the live bearer token to bedrock-key.env,
# which *.env above already covers. It writes it through tempfile.mkstemp in the
# same directory first, and that temp name matches neither *.env nor .env.*
# because the random suffix lands after the extension. The script unlinks it on
# any exception, so only a SIGKILL or a power loss leaves one behind, but the
# file that survives holds a live credential and git would otherwise offer it.
.*.env.*

# Local event-registration exports and generated Vocareum enrollment batches.
signup/vocareum-enrollment-8_27/
signup/*.csv
!signup/enroll-students.csv

